# Expectation record for 03_initializers/006_designated_mixed_nested.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 006_designated_mixed_nested
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Mixed positional and designated initializers inside nested aggregates -- six forms that force the C11 current object to be tracked correctly as the initializer descends into a brace, applies a designator, ascends and resumes positionally, three of them repeated at automatic storage duration; the OVERLAPPING-designator-at-depth spelling is excluded, narrowly and with its reason recorded in impl_defined_notes, because the frozen warning gate rejects every spelling of it
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
No uninitialized storage is read, which needs stating first because most of the values this program
prints are ones its initializers never mention. Every member or element left unmentioned by an
initializer is initialized as an object of static storage duration would be -- that is, to zero --
by C11 6.7.9p19 and p21, and that holds for automatic duration exactly as for static, because an
aggregate with ANY initializer is fully initialized. So g_pos_desig_in.in.p, the whole of
g_arr_pos_then_desig[1], all of row 1 and five of row 2 in g_m_pos_then_desig, g_deep_mixed.pr[0],
g_deep_desig.o.tag, o.in.q, o.trailer and pr[1].p, and the corresponding members of the automatic
twins all have determinate values of zero rather than indeterminate ones. That guarantee is the
feature under test, not an assumption of the test's.
Every designator names an existing member or an index strictly inside the declared bounds of the
aggregate it designates, and every positional initializer that follows a designator initializes the
subobject that follows the designated one, which C11 6.7.9p17 fixes. NO subobject in this program is
designated twice, so no initializer's answer turns on which of two writes to one slot happens last.
Order still matters, and C11 6.7.9p19 fixes it by initializing in initializer-list order: form 2's
unlabelled brace has to bind to the member following the designated one and its bare trailing value
has to continue on past it, and form 6's `.pr = { { 43, 44 }, [1].q = 46 }` mixes a positional
element with a combined index-and-member designator. That is a separate rule from
the sequencing of side effects, which C11 6.7.9p23 leaves indeterminate: a subobject initialized
twice by expressions WITH side effects would have an unspecified value, and mixing positional and
designated forms is exactly the shape in which that hazard is easiest to write by accident. Every
initializer expression in this program is an integer constant expression with no side effect at all,
so there is nothing for 6.7.9p23 to make unspecified and the program's meaning does not depend on
the order in which the list's side effects are sequenced. GCC's -Woverride-init-side-effects, which
is on by default and is not a gate member, is a second reason side-effecting initializers are
avoided here rather than suppressed.
No arithmetic is performed on any initialized value, so no signed overflow is reachable. The only
arithmetic is the loop counters' increments, bounded by the literals 3, 3 and 2. Nothing is shifted,
divided or remaindered. Nothing is modified after its initialization, so no object is modified twice
between two sequence points.
Every subscript stays strictly inside its bound, and each loop bound is a literal equal to the
declared extent: g_arr_pos_then_desig and l_arr_mixed are struct inner[3] read at 0 through 2,
g_m_pos_then_desig is int[3][3] read at [0..2][0..2], and every pr member is struct inner[2] read at
0 and 1. No pointer is formed anywhere in the program apart from printf's format argument, so no
one-past-the-end pointer exists to be dereferenced, no pointer arithmetic can leave an object, no
address is taken and none is printed.
There is no aliasing violation: every value is read through an lvalue of its own declared type,
which is int in every case, reached by member selection and subscripting only. No aggregate is
printed whole, no object representation is inspected, no union appears and no cast of any kind is
present in the file, so no padding byte is observed and nothing depends on the relative addresses of
unrelated objects.
Every initializer value is a small positive int, the largest being 76, so each is representable in
int on every target the suite supports and no implicit conversion changes a value.
Each printf call receives at most two loop counters and one int datum, none of which has a side
effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. %d is the only conversion specifier in the file and every corresponding argument has type
int after the default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns a constant 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system. Every input is a literal in this file: nothing is read from the
environment, the clock, the file system or the network, and iteration order is fixed by literal
bounds, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, with no diagnostic of any kind and no
source-level diagnostic suppression anywhere in the translation unit, and it builds and runs clean
under the sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched. One initializer spelling is excluded to reach that clean audit rather than suppressed
inside it, and the exclusion, its measured reason and which of the harder forms remain under test
are recorded in impl_defined_notes below.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing that the harness reads: all four targets, all three optimization
levels and all three oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, no gate
deviation is claimed under the ub_audit_flags key, and no implementation-defined value reaches
this program's output. One initializer SPELLING is nevertheless excluded from the source, and the
paragraph below states which, why, and which of the harder forms remain under test.
CONSTRAINT-C3 EXCLUSION -- THE OVERLAPPING-DESIGNATOR-AT-DEPTH SPELLING. Overriding a
designated initializer at DEPTH -- naming one nested subobject twice -- is well-defined C11
(6.7.9p19), and it would be worth testing separately from the flat override because the override
has to interact correctly with the current-object descent: an implementation that resolved
designators against the wrong nesting level would override a sibling, or the outer object, rather
than the subobject named. GCC nevertheless reports it under -Woverride-init, which -Wextra enables
and which the audit gate's -Werror makes fatal. FOURTEEN override spellings were MEASURED against
that gate with the reference compiler -- the flat and the nested ones alike, enumerated in
004_designated_array.c and in 004_designated_array.expected -- and every one is rejected, so no
spelling of that route exists that the unmodified gate accepts. An override carrying a side effect
is no escape either: -Woverride-init-side-effects is on by default and is not a gate member at all,
and C11 6.7.9p23 leaves the sequencing of an initializer list's side effects unspecified, which
requirement 1 forbids outright. No admissible deviation exists: the gate's removable members are
exactly -pedantic, for the GCC-extensions area, and -Wconversion with -Wsign-conversion, for the
deliberate narrowing program, so -Wextra is not removable and area 03 is granted no deviation at
all. A source-level diagnostic-suppression directive is not an alternative to that: it neutralizes
a gate member from inside the translation unit while this record still claims the unchanged gate,
which would make this record's own claim false rather than making the program clean. The spelling
is therefore dropped from the source, and constraint C3 is satisfied the way it asks to be -- the
exclusion is narrow, it is scoped to one spelling, it changes no target, no optimization level and
no oracle, and its reason is recorded here and in the program's own header comment. The specific
loss is the two nested overriding forms the file used to carry, one in each direction, which
together separated "last writer wins" from "any explicit member survives" at depth; that loss is
stated rather than left to be inferred, and it is a gap in this area that no program closes.
THREE GATE FACTS GOVERN THE SHAPE OF THESE INITIALIZERS and must not be disturbed by anyone editing
the program. First, -Wextra enables -Wmissing-field-initializers, which in C does not fire for a
designated initializer but does for a positional partial one, so every struct here that omits a
member omits it via a designator and every fully positional struct initializer supplies all of its
members; removing a designator would trip the gate. Second, -Wall enables -Wmissing-braces, so
every nested aggregate here is fully braced; eliding a brace would trip the gate as well. Third,
-Wextra enables -Woverride-init, so no initializer here may name a subobject an earlier one already
named -- which is the exclusion above. All three are honoured by writing gate-clean source rather
than by suppressing a diagnostic, and this translation unit contains no diagnostic-suppression
directive of any kind. Two neighbouring programs make the same choice for the same reason, so the
three exclusions across this area form a coherent set rather than three accidents:
003_partial_zero_fill.c excludes the positional partial STRUCT spelling, 002_nested_aggregate.c
excludes the brace-elided spelling, and 004_designated_array.c excludes the flat
overlapping-designator spelling. Each records its own reason in its own header and its own record.
WHAT REMAINS UNDER TEST IS THE HARDER HALF OF THE SAME QUESTION -- tracking the current object
through a descent -- which is why the exclusion is narrow rather than a retreat from the area's
mandate. Form 1 lands a value positionally, descends into a brace where a designator sets q and
leaves p zero, then resumes positionally on trailer. Form 2 designates tag, then an UNLABELLED
brace that must bind to the following member, then a bare value that must continue past it. Form 3
takes a positional element then a designated one, skipping the element between. Form 4 fills row 0
positionally and then jumps straight to [2][1], leaving five elements zero, so a designator landing
in the wrong row or column is immediately visible. Form 5 nests form 1 one level deeper beside a
designated sibling array. Form 6, the most demanding initializer in this area, spells
`.o = { .in.p = 42 }` -- two levels down, leaving o.tag, o.in.q and o.trailer zero -- alongside
`.pr = { { 43, 44 }, [1].q = 46 }`, a positional element followed by a combined index-and-member
designator. None of them names a slot twice, which is exactly why all six are gate-clean.
Forms 1, 3 and 5 are repeated at automatic storage duration, so the static-image path and the
run-time path are both exercised; form 3's twin uses the combined [2].q spelling rather than
[2] = { ... }. That pairing is the discriminating variant in this area and is why all three
optimization levels matter: with optimization off the statics appear as data-section bytes while
the twins appear as a run of stores into the frame, and at a higher level either path may be folded
into immediate operands. A volatile operand would add nothing, because the subject here is what an
initializer produces rather than what an operator computes.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every member is an int and %d is the only conversion specifier, so no target's
pointer or long width can be observed: i686 is ELF32 with a four-byte long and pointer while
x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64 are ELF64 with eight bytes for both
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462), and this program touches neither
type. No sizeof or _Alignof result is printed and no address is printed, so no layout choice the
ABI is free to make is observable.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. No character data appears at all, so the MEASURED split -- signed on x86-64
and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- cannot arise.
PADDING. Every member at every nesting level is read individually by name; no aggregate is printed
whole and no representation is inspected, so no padding byte is ever observed.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 57 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. The same twelve
configurations were re-measured after the excluded spelling was removed, so these 57 lines are the
current source's output rather than a residue of an earlier one. Nothing is summarized,
so one divergent line localizes the defect to one mixed form at one nesting level.
END
